1
00:00:13,384 --> 00:00:26,847
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is from Anguttara Nikaya, Book of Twos, verse 12, and this refrain is found in many suttas.

2
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:37,690
[SPEAKER_00]: The Buddha says, because I have personally known two things, non-contentment in regard to wholesome qualities and tireless striving.

3
00:00:43,632 --> 00:00:45,153
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the refrain that comes in.

4
00:00:45,193 --> 00:00:49,357
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, I strove tirelessly with this attitude in mind.

5
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:57,884
[SPEAKER_00]: Willingly, let only my skin, sinews and bones remain, and let the flesh and blood dry up in my body.

6
00:00:58,705 --> 00:01:06,931
[SPEAKER_00]: But I will not relax my energy, so long as I have not attained what can be attained by manly strength, energy and exertion.

7
00:01:08,012 --> 00:01:20,778
[SPEAKER_00]: And it was by that type of heedfulness that I achieved liberation, that I achieved unsurpassed security from bondage.

8
00:01:22,119 --> 00:01:23,459
[SPEAKER_01]: It comes down to the obvious.

9
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:30,443
[SPEAKER_01]: In order to do the right effort, you need to know what the right effort is.

10
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:33,804
[SPEAKER_01]: Because usually that very

11
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:46,574
[SPEAKER_01]: This passage is interpreted in a way that it just means this unwavering, blind determination.

12
00:01:47,095 --> 00:01:49,857
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, I just determine that I will not

13
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:54,582
[SPEAKER_01]: Move from here until I become enlightened.

14
00:01:54,602 --> 00:01:56,323
[SPEAKER_00]: Classic, like, I watch my breath.

15
00:01:56,864 --> 00:01:58,085
[SPEAKER_00]: I've heard about ānāpānasati.

16
00:01:58,105 --> 00:02:02,627
[SPEAKER_00]: So, now I'm going to focus on my breath until my knees pop out of their sockets.

17
00:02:02,647 --> 00:02:02,868
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

18
00:02:03,448 --> 00:02:06,770
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's misguided on various levels.

19
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:10,853
[SPEAKER_01]: First level being, so, do you know what enlightenment is?

20
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:12,493
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you know exactly?

21
00:02:13,274 --> 00:02:14,514
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I'm right here now.

22
00:02:15,215 --> 00:02:21,497
[SPEAKER_01]: My mind is free from this much and not free from these things and so on.

23
00:02:21,737 --> 00:02:23,978
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the work I need to do to be enlightened.

24
00:02:24,919 --> 00:02:28,540
[SPEAKER_01]: As Buddha would say, like, a person who understands, he knows what needs to be done.

25
00:02:29,361 --> 00:02:32,362
[SPEAKER_01]: He can see the extent of his mind that needs to be developed.

26
00:02:32,762 --> 00:02:36,043
[SPEAKER_01]: So, do you see that for yourself before you make a determination?

27
00:02:37,604 --> 00:02:38,044
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, okay.

28
00:02:38,064 --> 00:02:39,385
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is what I need to

29
00:02:40,899 --> 00:02:44,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Do and train to reach the complete enlightenment.

30
00:02:45,423 --> 00:02:47,424
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you realize, no, you don't know that.

31
00:02:48,005 --> 00:02:52,829
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, here you are determining that you will not move, breathe, or whatever else, until you become enlightened.

32
00:02:52,869 --> 00:02:57,813
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't know what enlightenment is, yet you're making determination towards enlightenment.

33
00:02:58,273 --> 00:03:02,156
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you... that's what means it's misguided, because, in a sense, your determination is real.

34
00:03:03,177 --> 00:03:05,419
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, there were people who fully committed to this,

35
00:03:07,658 --> 00:03:19,726
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, you commit out of this faith, that enlightenment will happen to you, if you exhibit unwavering determination, regardless of whether you know the goal or not.

36
00:03:20,227 --> 00:03:21,968
[SPEAKER_00]: You just want it hard enough.

37
00:03:22,028 --> 00:03:28,353
[SPEAKER_01]: I want it so much, that I will sacrifice my life, in hope that it will happen to me.

38
00:03:29,293 --> 00:03:30,474
[SPEAKER_01]: They will be given to me.

39
00:03:30,674 --> 00:03:32,155
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's not enlightenment already.

40
00:03:33,016 --> 00:03:35,638
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's when, when you read this passage, when the Buddha describes,

41
00:03:36,698 --> 00:03:42,700
[SPEAKER_01]: the let my sinews dry out, my blood dry up, and my up, like, just bones and sinews left, and so on.

42
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:52,203
[SPEAKER_01]: It's to the point of, ah, you know exactly what needs to be done, and you will not be... and you will not be careless in regard to that.

43
00:03:53,583 --> 00:03:55,064
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's what we said in other talks.

44
00:03:55,084 --> 00:03:59,425
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, for example, you recognize that a thought of sensuality is not your problem.

45
00:04:00,965 --> 00:04:08,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Accepting the thought of sensuality, welcoming, delighting in it, not seeing through it, not seeing the nature of it, that is your problem.

46
00:04:09,151 --> 00:04:10,312
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the problem is there.

47
00:04:11,052 --> 00:04:15,075
[SPEAKER_01]: So, now you kind of already are distinguishing where the work is.

48
00:04:15,315 --> 00:04:25,523
[SPEAKER_01]: The work is on the level of not entertaining sensuality, not being careless about it, not doing things that will bring sensuality to increase and non-sensuality to decrease.

49
00:04:26,831 --> 00:04:30,172
[SPEAKER_01]: And now, I will determine that I will not waver in that regard.

50
00:04:30,692 --> 00:04:39,636
[SPEAKER_01]: So, regardless of what scenario I'm in, what circumstances are there, whenever there is a central thought, I will not give in to it.

51
00:04:41,116 --> 00:04:52,000
[SPEAKER_01]: So, once you clarify what the work is, what needs to be done, what the training is, you make a determination that to that extent of the training, you will not compromise it.

52
00:04:53,085 --> 00:05:04,008
[SPEAKER_01]: That doesn't... and then you realize, okay, so that doesn't mean I need to sit and not breathe until I reach enlightenment and die, unless... No, it just means I know what the work is and I will never compromise on that knowledge.

53
00:05:04,408 --> 00:05:07,809
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly what... whatever is to be obtained by the manly effort.

54
00:05:08,569 --> 00:05:11,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Also, you... what can you do with the manly effort?

55
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:14,251
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you can do that which you know how to do.

56
00:05:14,971 --> 00:05:17,972
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't have manly effort, but you don't know what you're supposed to do with it.

57
00:05:19,413 --> 00:05:27,338
[SPEAKER_01]: So, with manly effort, manly restraint, with determination, with unwavering commitment, I will not tolerate sensuality.

58
00:05:29,059 --> 00:05:37,005
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to get rid of everything and die in some little hole, not eating and not drinking water until I become enlightened.

59
00:05:37,025 --> 00:05:37,145
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

60
00:05:37,645 --> 00:05:44,250
[SPEAKER_01]: But I will not tolerate sensuality, regardless of what circumstances throw at me, for the rest of my life.

61
00:05:45,582 --> 00:05:52,106
[SPEAKER_01]: I will not tolerate ill-will with a manly effort, manly restraint, manly commitment for the rest of my life.

62
00:05:53,707 --> 00:05:54,847
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, if it's non-ill-will, fine.

63
00:05:55,167 --> 00:05:56,989
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to train that, because it's not ill-will.

64
00:05:57,209 --> 00:05:58,890
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to train that, because it's not sensuality.

65
00:06:00,711 --> 00:06:08,635
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that entire thing that he determined was based upon fully discerned path of what needs to be done.

66
00:06:08,875 --> 00:06:13,678
[SPEAKER_01]: So, unless you know what needs to be done, your determination will be misguided.

67
00:06:15,152 --> 00:06:37,540
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you should then, instead of determining in that like a wishful way, oh, may my bones dry up and I will never move unless I become enlightened, whatever enlightenment might be, instead of doing that, which can be very intoxicating, because that determination, just making a blind determination is, yeah, it brings lots of energy behind it, so you can feel very good.

68
00:06:38,613 --> 00:06:41,215
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, yeah, but is it rooted in knowledge?

69
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:42,616
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it rooted in exactly what you need to do?

70
00:06:42,877 --> 00:06:44,218
[SPEAKER_01]: Or is it rooted in wishful thinking?

71
00:06:44,318 --> 00:06:48,041
[SPEAKER_01]: And as the Buddha said himself, the path cannot be obtained by wishing alone.

72
00:06:48,461 --> 00:06:49,622
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, may I become enlightened?

73
00:06:49,922 --> 00:06:51,964
[SPEAKER_01]: But yeah, are you doing the things that lead to enlightenment?

74
00:06:52,044 --> 00:06:52,685
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I don't know.

75
00:06:52,725 --> 00:06:54,326
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, then you won't become enlightened.

76
00:06:54,506 --> 00:07:00,111
[SPEAKER_00]: Someone said, I might not know what enlightenment is, or exactly how to get there.

77
00:07:00,151 --> 00:07:00,771
[SPEAKER_00]: There you go.

78
00:07:01,052 --> 00:07:04,454
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, instead of your determination being on that level,

79
00:07:05,375 --> 00:07:11,541
[SPEAKER_01]: When you don't even know what it is, why don't you scale it down a bit and actually apply it to things you can know?

80
00:07:12,221 --> 00:07:14,543
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so I don't know what enlightenment is.

81
00:07:14,563 --> 00:07:18,567
[SPEAKER_01]: How about I determine, I will not rest until I find out what enlightenment is.

82
00:07:20,048 --> 00:07:20,468
[SPEAKER_01]: There you go.

83
00:07:20,689 --> 00:07:21,589
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your work already.

84
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:23,011
[SPEAKER_01]: Find out.

85
00:07:23,171 --> 00:07:31,018
[SPEAKER_01]: Not entertain wishful thinking about enlightenment will happen to me on account of these random practices that I took on faith and mere faith alone.

86
00:07:33,539 --> 00:07:36,480
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, you start... how do... how do you know what enlightenment is?

87
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, start reading the Buddha's words.

88
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:39,800
[SPEAKER_01]: Start thinking about it.

89
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:40,681
[SPEAKER_01]: Start reflecting it.

90
00:07:40,741 --> 00:07:45,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Start questioning what you understood and removing, basically, layer by layer by layer.

91
00:07:46,742 --> 00:07:50,343
[SPEAKER_01]: Determine that until you know that you know, you will not rest.

92
00:07:50,643 --> 00:07:52,523
[SPEAKER_01]: Until you get the right view, you will not rest.

93
00:07:52,863 --> 00:07:54,684
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't mean you'll never sleep.

94
00:07:54,744 --> 00:07:57,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't mean... means you will never forget that that is your goal.

95
00:07:59,505 --> 00:08:01,145
[SPEAKER_01]: You will never sit down and say,

96
00:08:02,810 --> 00:08:05,511
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I won't think about the dhamma now.

97
00:08:06,991 --> 00:08:09,512
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because I have something else to do, it's simply because I don't want to.

98
00:08:15,293 --> 00:08:17,554
[SPEAKER_01]: You won't do that, because you're determined to not do that.

99
00:08:19,314 --> 00:08:21,075
[SPEAKER_01]: So when you can, you will do it.

100
00:08:22,997 --> 00:08:33,265
[SPEAKER_01]: You will reflect, you will learn, and then you'll get to know what enlightenment is, and then you'll know what you need to do, and then you apply the same type of determination to exactly the right extent, the middle way.

101
00:08:34,106 --> 00:08:39,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Not too much to the point of, as the Buddha himself tried before, I'll stop breathing and I'll die.

102
00:08:40,712 --> 00:08:44,955
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that was an ignoble way, as ignorant as sensuality is.

103
00:08:46,416 --> 00:08:48,518
[SPEAKER_00]: It's conceited.

104
00:08:48,538 --> 00:08:49,158
[SPEAKER_01]: Fully, fully.

105
00:08:49,359 --> 00:08:50,900
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing really gets uprooted there.

106
00:08:53,237 --> 00:08:58,620
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you want to discern the extent of the training, what the actual training is.

107
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:04,122
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, this is a training, okay, but do I see that for myself or have I just repeated what I heard from somebody else?

108
00:09:04,963 --> 00:09:13,087
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if that thing is right thing that you heard from somebody else, okay, so you're doing it, but are you seeing now how that is the training?

109
00:09:13,867 --> 00:09:15,548
[SPEAKER_01]: To what extent your mind is trained?

110
00:09:16,792 --> 00:09:18,193
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is your responsibility with it?

111
00:09:18,553 --> 00:09:25,699
[SPEAKER_01]: The clearer you become about that, the clearer will... the easier will be to determine the right effort towards it.

112
00:09:26,479 --> 00:09:31,082
[SPEAKER_01]: The only reason people can't determine the effort towards enlightenment, is because they don't have a clue what it is.

113
00:09:31,423 --> 00:09:33,164
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't even know when... where to start.

114
00:09:34,905 --> 00:09:45,633
[SPEAKER_01]: And you... as you know yourself, whenever you want to try, like, learning new things, beginning is always the hardest, because you can't even master that strength to begin, because you just imagine all this... you don't know anything about it.

115
00:09:46,862 --> 00:09:49,844
[SPEAKER_01]: But instead of projecting... like, you want to learn a new language.

116
00:09:49,944 --> 00:10:00,452
[SPEAKER_01]: Instead of projecting, like, your determination on the level of being fluent, how about I maybe just make a determination to spend five minutes of reading the other language a day?

117
00:10:00,673 --> 00:10:01,293
[SPEAKER_01]: No more than that.

118
00:10:01,413 --> 00:10:02,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Just five minutes.

119
00:10:02,314 --> 00:10:03,895
[SPEAKER_01]: But do it consistently.

120
00:10:05,456 --> 00:10:06,777
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter what comes out of it.

121
00:10:06,877 --> 00:10:07,598
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just do this.

122
00:10:10,085 --> 00:10:12,207
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, before you know it, you're much more familiar.

123
00:10:12,267 --> 00:10:22,098
[SPEAKER_01]: The more familiar you become, the new options, the new ways of furthering that training will present themselves now, because you actually started building it up from the right level, from the bottom up.

124
00:10:22,838 --> 00:10:26,522
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like, I don't know, anything in between, me and enlightenment.

125
00:10:26,923 --> 00:10:32,809
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just determine the enlightenment and then wish it will happen to me, missing all the other steps in between.

126
00:10:36,866 --> 00:10:40,427
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why, as the Buddha said, it cannot be obtained by the wishing alone.

127
00:10:40,987 --> 00:10:42,108
[SPEAKER_01]: It just doesn't work like that.

128
00:10:44,208 --> 00:10:49,850
[SPEAKER_00]: And the first thing he said, I knew non-contentment with wholesome qualities.

129
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:50,630
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the thing.

130
00:10:50,911 --> 00:11:00,494
[SPEAKER_01]: But not knowing really what the training is, not knowing what the wholesome is, you will be discontent in the face of wholesome.

131
00:11:02,354 --> 00:11:04,355
[SPEAKER_01]: You haven't learned the content of the wholesome.

132
00:11:05,362 --> 00:11:06,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't see it for what it is.

133
00:11:11,204 --> 00:11:13,664
[SPEAKER_01]: And then consequently, you will be content with the unwholesome.

134
00:11:14,224 --> 00:11:16,745
[SPEAKER_01]: With the actually harmful for you, you'll be content.

135
00:11:16,765 --> 00:11:18,486
[SPEAKER_00]: He was non-content with the wholesome qualities.

136
00:11:18,506 --> 00:11:24,387
[SPEAKER_01]: He was non-content with the wholesome qualities, because the contentment out of the wholesome will not come automatically.

137
00:11:24,927 --> 00:11:27,588
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to develop it on account of sticking to the wholesome.

138
00:11:28,807 --> 00:11:29,828
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it's so hard.

139
00:11:30,208 --> 00:11:34,852
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why, as I said so many times before, you cannot arrive at the dhamma accidentally.

140
00:11:35,232 --> 00:11:38,595
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, see, you got the wholesome thing, but it doesn't feel right.

141
00:11:39,556 --> 00:11:40,957
[SPEAKER_01]: You're discontent about it.

142
00:11:42,438 --> 00:11:47,522
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you discern that it's the right thing, as the Buddha himself did, and he stuck to it,

143
00:11:49,155 --> 00:11:51,217
[SPEAKER_01]: The contentment arose from it.

144
00:11:51,457 --> 00:11:52,738
[SPEAKER_01]: And then it was effortless.

145
00:11:53,118 --> 00:11:54,880
[SPEAKER_01]: Then the tireless energy arises.

146
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,961
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's the energy you are not making.

147
00:11:57,362 --> 00:12:01,025
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the energy that's discerning the things.

148
00:12:01,185 --> 00:12:03,086
[SPEAKER_01]: Like we spoke before, the effortless mindfulness.

149
00:12:03,126 --> 00:12:05,188
[SPEAKER_01]: If mindfulness is done correctly, it is effortless.

150
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:07,450
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't require your determination.

151
00:12:08,368 --> 00:12:10,049
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're holding on and doing it.

152
00:12:10,149 --> 00:12:17,714
[SPEAKER_01]: It's effortless because it's in the things themselves, in the nature of awareness, the nature of being alive, it already has a degree of mindfulness in it.

153
00:12:17,754 --> 00:12:25,939
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's discerning that and tapping into that, on account of right restraint, right effort, rounding it up, building it up, then it's effortless.

154
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,121
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you can't have too much of it or too little of it.

155
00:12:29,181 --> 00:12:31,723
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just effortless because it's just part of the experience as a whole.

156
00:12:34,822 --> 00:12:37,143
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, when...

157
00:12:37,463 --> 00:12:43,126
[SPEAKER_00]: I suppose most people read that, you know, let my bones, my blood dry up and so on.

158
00:12:43,406 --> 00:12:44,727
[SPEAKER_00]: It means like ascetic practice.

159
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:48,288
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it means this intense... and you can take it away.

160
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:57,152
[SPEAKER_01]: And it could... it might be wholesome, but wholesomeness or usefulness of it will not be determined by your determination or by the extent of determination.

161
00:12:57,493 --> 00:13:02,555
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be determined by the... whether you know what enlightenment is, what the training is, or you don't know.

162
00:13:03,523 --> 00:13:08,684
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why for some people, the Buddha said, by all means, you have to do these ascetic practices.

163
00:13:10,184 --> 00:13:12,065
[SPEAKER_01]: But for some people, you shouldn't.

164
00:13:13,145 --> 00:13:16,766
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not measured by you deciding whether you should or shouldn't.

165
00:13:16,926 --> 00:13:21,487
[SPEAKER_01]: It's measured by you knowing what enlightenment is, and then seeing what supports it and what doesn't support it.

166
00:13:23,187 --> 00:13:28,748
[SPEAKER_01]: What supports maintenance of that middle way, and what kind of overshoots it or undershoots it.

167
00:13:29,835 --> 00:13:31,176
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the measure is the knowledge.

168
00:13:31,416 --> 00:13:37,921
[SPEAKER_01]: The measure of your determination is the knowledge of the path, the right view, what enlightenment is.

169
00:13:39,362 --> 00:13:40,583
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you'll know to what extent.

170
00:13:40,603 --> 00:13:51,610
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why he did not... when those monks, Devadatta asked him to make these ascetic practices, which are very, like, noble and lofty, to make them mandatory for every monk.

171
00:13:51,890 --> 00:13:52,591
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha said, no.

172
00:13:53,111 --> 00:13:55,433
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, actually, they would be detrimental for some monks.

173
00:13:57,145 --> 00:14:05,007
[SPEAKER_01]: Some mind, once they know the Enlightenment, if they go too far into ascetic, they will obscure the right level of training of Enlightenment.

174
00:14:05,087 --> 00:14:06,787
[SPEAKER_01]: They will not approve the Ukyalesa.

175
00:14:08,088 --> 00:14:12,649
[SPEAKER_01]: Some mind, if they know the Enlightenment, they need the ascetic level to reach their right threshold.

176
00:14:12,949 --> 00:14:15,030
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it cannot be made as a blanket rule.

177
00:14:15,330 --> 00:14:16,270
[SPEAKER_01]: You all must do this.

178
00:14:16,450 --> 00:14:17,390
[SPEAKER_01]: You all must do that.

179
00:14:18,571 --> 00:14:22,271
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, literally, not two minds are the same.

180
00:14:22,612 --> 00:14:24,052
[SPEAKER_01]: Not two minds are on the same level.

181
00:14:24,789 --> 00:14:30,514
[SPEAKER_00]: I think in society now, it errs on the side of indulgence, you know.

182
00:14:30,534 --> 00:14:32,015
[SPEAKER_00]: You're way too comfortable.

183
00:14:32,675 --> 00:14:33,336
[SPEAKER_00]: Ascetic practices...

184
00:14:33,356 --> 00:14:33,536
[SPEAKER_00]: It does.

185
00:14:33,756 --> 00:14:34,056
[SPEAKER_01]: It does.

186
00:14:34,177 --> 00:14:39,921
[SPEAKER_01]: And no, well, ascetic practices always, even back in the time, back in the Buddha's day, were always more inspiring.

187
00:14:41,242 --> 00:14:41,963
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what Buddha said.

188
00:14:42,443 --> 00:14:50,970
[SPEAKER_01]: If you can do the ascetic practices without compromising the level of training for enlightenment, you are practicing for the future generations.

189
00:14:51,527 --> 00:14:55,632
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, future generations are not going to be inspired on account of enlightenment, because they don't have a clue what that is.

190
00:14:56,033 --> 00:14:58,356
[SPEAKER_01]: But they will be inspired on account of your ascetic practice.

191
00:14:58,636 --> 00:14:59,438
[SPEAKER_01]: And you always see that.

192
00:14:59,478 --> 00:15:01,640
[SPEAKER_01]: Whenever somebody is ascetic, it's always more inspirational.

193
00:15:02,261 --> 00:15:03,022
[SPEAKER_01]: That's just factual.

194
00:15:03,283 --> 00:15:06,347
[SPEAKER_01]: But it doesn't necessarily mean that on the individual level it's more wholesome.

195
00:15:07,105 --> 00:15:09,847
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, sensuality must be abandoned one way or the other.

196
00:15:10,568 --> 00:15:16,011
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when we say that sometimes asceticism is not wholesome, it doesn't mean, oh, so yeah, I can just stay in sensuality.

197
00:15:16,092 --> 00:15:16,812
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

198
00:15:17,573 --> 00:15:18,954
[SPEAKER_01]: That's completely the other level.

199
00:15:19,174 --> 00:15:20,615
[SPEAKER_01]: They must be abandoned through and through.

200
00:15:20,775 --> 00:15:22,676
[SPEAKER_00]: Like celibacy is not an option.

201
00:15:22,996 --> 00:15:24,137
[SPEAKER_01]: Celibacy is not optional.

202
00:15:24,217 --> 00:15:27,460
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when we talk about asceticism, we're not talking about the eight precepts.

203
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:44,877
[SPEAKER_01]: We're talking about taking the eight precepts on a whole new level, of like eating just an unharced rice, one handful of it, wearing rag robes, sleeping under... never sleeping under a roof, root of a tree, never taking medicine, never laying down,

204
00:15:46,518 --> 00:15:47,919
[SPEAKER_01]: Those are the ascetic practices.

205
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:55,386
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, that's a good point, because in some lesson they might confuse, thinking, oh, I mustn't go into asceticism too much, thus I don't have to be celibate.

206
00:15:55,587 --> 00:15:56,688
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's absolutely...

207
00:15:57,028 --> 00:15:59,951
[SPEAKER_01]: Eight precepts is the minimum for training towards the enlightenment.

208
00:16:00,872 --> 00:16:07,858
[SPEAKER_01]: Five precepts is the minimum for basically distinguishing yourself from an animal behavior, as the Buddha said, like a wholesome

209
00:16:09,179 --> 00:16:14,781
[SPEAKER_01]: Worldly behavior that does not lead to enlightenment, just leads to wholesome behavior and wholesome kamma and wholesome results of kamma.

210
00:16:15,322 --> 00:16:20,083
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you want to practice the words of enlightenment and train for it, eight precepts is the minimum.

211
00:16:21,404 --> 00:16:28,507
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, eight precepts for somebody who want to really be fully enlightened, as the line says, might not be enough.

212
00:16:29,607 --> 00:16:31,988
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it doesn't mean you introduce 16 precepts in 54.

213
00:16:32,328 --> 00:16:36,870
[SPEAKER_01]: It just means the principles of the eight precepts, now you need to amplify even more.

214
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:41,369
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, not sleep, laying down.

215
00:16:44,071 --> 00:16:50,796
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, not out of... because you read that such and such great Ajahn did that, and you were inspired to, like, show how manly you are, and I know.

216
00:16:51,197 --> 00:16:59,182
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because you actually see that laying down always makes you wake up with lust, carelessness, anger, and then takes you four hours to undo it.

217
00:16:59,703 --> 00:17:01,084
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what if I don't lay down?

218
00:17:02,945 --> 00:17:03,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah, there you go.

219
00:17:04,086 --> 00:17:06,668
[SPEAKER_01]: You got a practical basis for your ascetic practice.

220
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,141
[SPEAKER_01]: But, based on knowledge, what needs to be developed.

221
00:17:10,982 --> 00:17:30,532
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you don't have the knowledge for yourself, clearly, distinguished, free from doubt, what needs to be developed, any of these determination practices will be utterly misguided and all gonna amplify your conceit, as they did to every single ascetic giant back in the day that the Buddha mocked and said they were completely wrong and misguided.

222
00:17:31,738 --> 00:17:36,120
[SPEAKER_01]: So, instead, your determination should be pointed to that which you know that you can develop.

223
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:39,041
[SPEAKER_01]: Such as, I can become familiar with all the suttas.

224
00:17:40,382 --> 00:17:46,905
[SPEAKER_01]: My determination can basically make me read all the suttas daily and make the effort.

225
00:17:47,025 --> 00:17:52,468
[SPEAKER_01]: And when I finish, I start again, and again, and again, until I get the clarity of the message.

226
00:17:53,168 --> 00:17:54,989
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, you do need determination for that.

227
00:17:55,709 --> 00:17:56,390
[SPEAKER_01]: To do it every day.

228
00:17:57,370 --> 00:17:59,411
[SPEAKER_01]: To read it, and read it, and read it.

229
00:18:00,507 --> 00:18:03,689
[SPEAKER_01]: To familiarize yourself with Pali, you need determination for that.

230
00:18:04,369 --> 00:18:06,710
[SPEAKER_01]: To keep the precepts, you need determination for that.

231
00:18:07,050 --> 00:18:15,835
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all these things, you can actually have a vast amount of effort applied, full on determination, and not as misguided.

232
00:18:16,275 --> 00:18:22,738
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can actually develop this, you know, waiting for enlightenment to happen, on account of, I'll just never do this, never do this, never do that.

233
00:18:23,438 --> 00:18:26,560
[SPEAKER_01]: For no practical basis, you don't see the reason why you shouldn't do that.

234
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,841
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll never lay down.

235
00:18:31,341 --> 00:18:32,882
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but why?

236
00:18:32,902 --> 00:18:36,944
[SPEAKER_01]: Is laying down unwholesome like having a sexual intercourse, lying or killing?

237
00:18:38,005 --> 00:18:38,465
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, no.

238
00:18:38,625 --> 00:18:41,727
[SPEAKER_01]: So, where is your determination based upon?

239
00:18:41,747 --> 00:18:42,187
[SPEAKER_01]: Based in.

240
00:18:43,728 --> 00:18:44,389
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean.

241
00:18:44,529 --> 00:18:45,830
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no practice without the right view.

242
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:50,272
[SPEAKER_01]: We said it millions of times before.

243
00:18:51,813 --> 00:18:57,476
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you determining the end game of the practice without even knowing what the practice is, it's just contradiction in terms.

